# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit `.env` — it is gitignored (.gitignore lines 2-3).
#
# `.env` is the single source of truth for API keys in this project. setup.sh sources it at
# container build, which feeds both:
#   - the MCP server registrations (`fred`, `alpha-vantage`) in ~/.claude.json, and
#   - the ~/.bashrc exports that os.environ consumers (fredapi, the data pipelines) read.
# Rotating a key = edit `.env`, re-run `bash setup.sh`. Nothing else to update.
#
# Why here and not the host environment: `${localEnv:X}` in devcontainer.json reads the VS Code
# *server process* environment, which carries neither key — so remoteEnv passes nothing, and
# exporting from ~/.bashrc on the host does not help. The repo is bind-mounted, so this file is
# visible on the host and inside the container with no extra mount.
#
# Streamlit Community Cloud needs NEITHER key: app/ never calls FRED or Alpha Vantage at runtime,
# it reads pre-built parquet. Do not add these to Cloud secrets.

# https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
FRED_API_KEY=

# https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=
